}

docs {
  # GET /topics
  
  Retrieves topic modules for a course.
  
  ## HTTP Method & Route
  - **Method:** `GET`
  - **Route:** `/wp-json/tutor/v1/topics`
  
  ## Authentication
  - **With API key:** Bearer JWT (`Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}` or `Tutor-User-Token`) — user must be able to view the course (enrolled / instructor / public).
  - **Without API key:** allowed only when the course is **public**.
  - **Required Permission (API key):** `Read`, `Read/Write`, or `All`
  
  ## Query Parameters
  
  | Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
  | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
  | `course_id` | `integer` | **Yes** | Parent course post ID. |
  
  ## Notes
  
  Full topic bodies (`post_content`) are returned only when the caller may reveal learning payloads (enrolled / instructor / public free course). Otherwise topics are outline-only: `ID`, `post_title`, `post_name`.
  
  ## Responses
  
  ### 200 OK (Success)
  ```json
  {
    "code": "tutor_read_topic",
    "message": "Topic retrieved successfully",
    "data": [
      {
        "ID": 201,
        "post_title": "Getting Started with the Environment",
        "post_content": "Detailed overview of tools, IDE plugins, and prerequisites.",
        "post_name": "getting-started-environment"
      }
    ]
  }
  ```
  
  ### Missing `course_id`
  ```json
  {
    "code": "tutor_read_topic",
    "message": "course_id is required",
    "data": []
  }
  ```
  
  ### No topics
  ```json
  {
    "code": "tutor_read_topic",
    "message": "Topic not found for given course ID",
    "data": []
  }
  ```
}
